Z||000009||Cliff Pennock||10-09-2001||02:31 AM||||Well, <B>this is weird, very weird</B>... The forum <B>is</B> down at this very moment. In fact, my complete server is down at this moment so I have no clue whatsoever where this ghost forum is coming from. I had shut down the server yesterday to get rid of the "Internal error" and it wouldn't reboot (it sometimes does that). The only way I can solve that is to physically switch off the server and turn it back up again. Since it was 2am, I didn't have access to the server.<P>Then all of a sudden, I was getting emails from people everything was fine again, and I was like  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">? So I tried it, and lo and behold, the server was still down. Then I did some pings and traceroutes from the States and much to my suprise, I could reach the server just fine. I'm now posting through a server in the States and I'm completely flabbergasted.<P>Again, I have no clue how this is possible and I can't wait to reach the tech guys at my ISP.<P>Maybe the forum will only die if you cut of its head with a sword or something.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000010||Monkeyman||10-09-2001||03:18 AM||||Leave it to Cliff to find a way to get the forum up even when it's "impossible".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cliff Pennock||10-09-2001||05:04 AM||||Well, I found out why the forum was up while I thought it was down. Of course, the server was up and running just fine (and so was the forum) only it thought that my ip-address at home belonged to its local network. So it was receiving my requests, it was just sending out its response through the wrong network interface.<P>So <B>everybody</B> was able to reach the server <B>except me</B>.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Well, like, duh!||||reg||1
